// Math demo: LaTeX equations typeset to self-contained inline SVG at
// build time by RaTeX — no JavaScript, no webfonts. The glyph outlines
// are embedded as paths, so equations render offline (file://) and
// paint with `currentColor`, following the page text colour + theme.
//
// Authoring: the equation goes in the block's inline-label slot, so a
// raw heredoc (`<<'TEX'`) pastes backslash-heavy LaTeX verbatim — no
// escaping. (Every block still takes a `{}` body, hence the trailing
// braces after a heredoc.) Quoted strings suit backslash-free snippets.
// In prose, use `$…$` (text style) or `$$…$$` (display style); a span
// that contains backslash commands must itself be a raw heredoc.

page math { sites = [:showcase]
  h1 "Math equations" {}

  text {
    span "Equations render to self-contained SVG with embedded glyph outlines, so they work offline and follow the page's text colour and theme." {}
  }

  h2 "Inline math" {}
  text {
    span "Mass–energy equivalence $E = mc^2$ and the Pythagorean theorem $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ sit inline at the text baseline. Currency like $10 or $20 is left untouched." {}
  }
  text {
    span <<'S'
      Backslash commands need a raw-heredoc span: the sum $\sum_{i=1}^{n} i = \frac{n(n+1)}{2}$ flows with the prose.
      S
    {}
  }

  h2 "Inline display math" {}
  text {
    span <<'S'
      Set off mid-paragraph in display style with $$\int_0^1 x^2 \, dx = \tfrac{1}{3}$$ — larger operators, same line.
      S
    {}
  }

  h2 "Block equations" {}
  text { span "A `math` block is a centred display equation. A backslash-free one-liner:" {} }
  math "E = mc^2" {}

  text { span "Or a raw heredoc, pasted verbatim — no escaping:" {} }
  math <<'TEX'
    \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
    TEX
  {}

  math <<'TEX'
    \int_0^\infty e^{-x^2}\,dx = \frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2}
    TEX
  {}

  h2 "Theming" {}
  text { span "Equations paint with `currentColor`, so they inherit the text colour; an explicit `\\textcolor` overrides it:" {} }
  math <<'TEX'
    \textcolor{e06c75}{E} = \textcolor{61afef}{m}\textcolor{98c379}{c}^2
    TEX
  {}

  h2 "Malformed input degrades gracefully" {}
  text {
    span <<'S'
      A broken equation like $\frac{$ renders as an inline marker — it never fails the build.
      S
    {}
  }

  text { span "Back to [the index](index)." {} }
}
